  "description": "VOHKAH crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C128 H120 N12 O16 Sm4,4(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Sm1 (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm2 (Sm) has 6 O neighbors; Sm1A (Sm) has 7 O neighbors; Sm2A (Sm) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.651-3.927 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.81-112.74°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C136H132N16O16Sm4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
